  "interpretation": "The repeated vacuum yaw pulses show a mean absolute roll/yaw acceleration ratio of 0.385. The full-vessel inertia predicts 0.036 for a pure body-z yaw torque, about 10.7 times smaller. The captured off-diagonal inertia alone does not explain the cross-axis response. Applying the full three-axis Euler relation to the measured slopes implies an input-correlated body-roll torque of about 3.1% of the yaw torque in both pulse directions; this is inferred net torque, not a direct wheel measurement, and its actuator source remains unresolved. The recorded body_rates values are already degrees/s, as specified by the captured probe source; radians/s\u00b2 equivalents are provided separately. This does not identify the control-frame or actuator cause and is not atmospheric coordination or flight qualification.",
